        " صَلاَتِهِ وَ ثَوْبُهُ عَلَى فِيهِ فَقَالَ «لاَ بَأْسَ بِذَلِكَ. وَ فِي رِوَايَةِ اَلْحَلَبِيِّ: «إِذَا سَمِعَ اَلْهَمْهَمَةَ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.823 - Al-Halabi and Abdullah ibn Sinan asked Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) whether a man may recite during prayer with his garment covering his mouth.\nThe Imam said: \"There is no issue with that.\"\nIn another narration by Al-Halabi, it is added: \"As long as he can hear his murmuring (sound of his recitation)”."
        ]
      }
